#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-simple-table.php:24
msgid "Create Simple Table"
msgstr "Crea una tabella semplice"

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-simple-table.php:25
msgid "Creates a Simple wpDataTable (Handsontable editor, pure HTML, no sorting/filtering). Use when: static or manually curated content, heavy styling (pricing cards, comparison tables, pedigree). Do not use for external URLs or SQL-backed data. For images use {\"attachment_id\":123,\"size\":\"medium\",\"alt\":\"...\"} in cells; get IDs via list-media or upload-media-from-url. For styled tables use {\"data\":\"<div class='panel'>...</div>\",\"meta\":[]} and custom_css. Supports merged_cells, table_settings. WHEN TO CALL: user wants a designed/layout-heavy HTML table, pricing comparison, pedigree chart, or any non-data-source static content. DO NOT USE for: CSV/JSON/API data (use create-table-from-source), database queries (use create-table-from-query), or large sortable datasets. REQUIRED INPUT: title (string), columns (string[] headers). OPTIONAL: rows (array of row arrays — omit or pass [] to create an empty table skeleton for later editing in wp-admin), table_settings, merged_cells, custom_css. FOR IMAGES: first call list-media or upload-media-from-url, then put attachment_id in cell objects. RETURNS: table_id and shortcode. NEXT STEPS: update-simple-table-styles to refine layout; get-table-info to verify."
msgstr "Crea una semplice wpDataTable (editor Handsontable, puro HTML, senza ordinamento/filtraggio). Da usare quando: contenuti statici o curati manualmente, stile complesso (schede prezzi, tabelle comparative, alberi genealogici). Non usare per URL esterni o dati basati su SQL. Per le immagini usare {\"attachment_id\":123,\"size\":\"medium\",\"alt\":\"...\"} nelle celle; ottenere gli ID tramite list-media o upload-media-from-url. Per le tabelle stilizzate usare {\"data\":\"<div class='panel'>...</div>\",\"meta\":[]} e custom_css. Supporta merged_cells, table_settings. QUANDO CHIAMARE: l&#39;utente desidera una tabella HTML con un design complesso/layout elaborato, un confronto prezzi, un grafico genealogico o qualsiasi contenuto statico non proveniente da una sorgente dati. NON USARE per: dati CSV/JSON/API (usare create-table-from-source), query di database (usare create-table-from-query) o grandi set di dati ordinabili. INPUT OBBLIGATORIO: titolo (stringa), colonne (intestazioni string[]). OPZIONALE: righe (array di array di righe — omettere o passare [] per creare uno scheletro di tabella vuoto per la successiva modifica in wp-admin), table_settings, merged_cells, custom_css. PER LE IMMAGINI: prima chiamare list-media o upload-media-from-url, quindi inserire attachment_id negli oggetti cella. RESTITUISCE: table_id e shortcode. PASSAGGI SUCCESSIVI: update-simple-table-styles per perfezionare il layout; get-table-info per verificare."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-simple-table.php:91
msgid "For static HTML tables only. Obtain image attachment_id via list-media or upload-media-from-url before referencing images in cells. Do not use for file, API, or SQL data sources."
msgstr "Solo per tabelle HTML statiche. Ottenere l&#39;ID dell&#39;allegato dell&#39;immagine tramite list-media o upload-media-from-url prima di fare riferimento alle immagini nelle celle. Non utilizzare per origini dati file, API o SQL."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-simple-table.php:113
msgid "wpDataTables core classes WPDataTableRows and WDTConfigController are required."
msgstr "Sono necessarie le classi principali di wpDataTables, ovvero WPDataTableRows e WDTConfigController."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-simple-table.php:122
msgid "rows must be an array."
msgstr "Le righe devono essere un array."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-simple-table.php:130
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:363
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-source.php:364
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/import-table-from-source.php:125
msgid "title is required."
msgstr "Il titolo è obbligatorio."

#. translators: %d: row index
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-simple-table.php:246
#, php-format
msgid "rows[%d] must be an array of cells."
msgstr "rows[%d] deve essere un array di celle."

#. translators: 1: row index, 2: cell index
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-simple-table.php:258
#, php-format
msgid "rows[%1$d][%2$d] must be a string, number, boolean, null, or cell object."
msgstr "rows[%1$d][%2$d] deve essere una stringa, un numero, un valore booleano, null o un oggetto cella."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-simple-table.php:290
msgid "Failed to create table in database."
msgstr "Impossibile creare la tabella nel database."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:25
msgid "Create Table from SQL Query"
msgstr "Creare una tabella da una query SQL"

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:26
msgid "Creates a DataTable from a SQL SELECT query. Use when: data comes from the database (MySQL, MSSQL, PostgreSQL). Provides sorting, filtering, server-side processing. Do not use for external URLs or static HTML. First use list-db-tables and describe-db-table to inspect schemas. Only SELECT queries accepted; INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/DROP rejected. FROM must reference a simple table (no subqueries or derived tables). WHEN TO CALL: user wants a wpDataTable backed by database data with sorting/filtering. DO NOT USE for: files, APIs, or static HTML. CHECK get-system-info for tier and connection support. REQUIRED INPUT: title (string), query (SELECT only, e.g. SELECT * FROM wp_posts). OPTIONAL: connection (empty = WordPress DB), server_side (boolean, default true for large tables). TYPICAL WORKFLOW: get-system-info → list-db-tables → describe-db-table → create-table-from-query. RETURNS: table_id and shortcode. NEXT STEPS: get-table-info, update-table-settings, get-table-data (use search/column_search if server_side=true)."
msgstr "Crea una DataTable da una query SQL SELECT. Da usare quando: i dati provengono dal database (MySQL, MSSQL, PostgreSQL). Fornisce ordinamento, filtraggio ed elaborazione lato server. Non utilizzare per URL esterni o HTML statico. Utilizzare prima list-db-tables e describe-db-table per ispezionare gli schemi. Sono accettate solo query SELECT; INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/DROP sono rifiutati. FROM deve fare riferimento a una tabella semplice (nessuna sottoquery o tabella derivata). QUANDO CHIAMARE: l&#39;utente desidera una wpDataTable supportata da dati di database con ordinamento/filtraggio. NON UTILIZZARE per: file, API o HTML statico. CONTROLLARE get-system-info per il supporto di tier e connessione. INPUT OBBLIGATORIO: titolo (stringa), query (solo SELECT, ad esempio SELECT * FROM wp_posts). OPZIONALE: connessione (vuoto = DB di WordPress), server_side (booleano, predefinito true per tabelle di grandi dimensioni). FLUSSO DI LAVORO TIPICO: get-system-info → list-db-tables → describe-db-table → create-table-from-query. RESTITUISCE: table_id e shortcode. PASSAGGI SUCCESSIVI: get-table-info, update-table-settings, get-table-data (utilizzare search/column_search se server_side=true)."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:72
msgid "SELECT queries only. Use list-db-tables and describe-db-table first. Set server_side=true for tables with more than ~1000 rows."
msgstr "Solo query SELECT. Utilizzare prima list-db-tables e describe-db-table. Impostare server_side=true per le tabelle con più di ~1000 righe."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:128
msgid "SQL parser is not available; cannot validate the query."
msgstr "Il parser SQL non è disponibile; impossibile convalidare la query."

#. translators: %s: Parser error message
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:141
#, php-format
msgid "Query could not be parsed: %s"
msgstr "Impossibile analizzare la query: %s"

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:163
msgid "UNION queries are not permitted. Use a single SELECT statement."
msgstr "Le query UNION non sono consentite. Utilizzare una singola istruzione SELECT."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:170
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:238
msgid "Only SELECT queries are allowed. INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, DROP, TRUNCATE, CREATE, ALTER, EXPLAIN, DESCRIBE, and UNION are not permitted."
msgstr "Sono consentite solo le query SELECT. Le query INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, DROP, TRUNCATE, CREATE, ALTER, EXPLAIN, DESCRIBE e UNION non sono consentite."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:178
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:217
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:246
msgid "Query must be a SELECT statement."
msgstr "La query deve essere un&#39;istruzione SELECT."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:198
msgid "Only a single SELECT statement is allowed. Multiple statements separated by semicolons are not permitted."
msgstr "È consentita una sola istruzione SELECT. Non sono ammesse più istruzioni separate da punti e virgola."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:265
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:366
msgid "query is required."
msgstr "È necessaria una query."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:285
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:316
msgid "Query could not be parsed."
msgstr "Impossibile analizzare la query."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:323
msgid "Query must have a FROM clause with a table reference."
msgstr "La query deve includere una clausola FROM con un riferimento alla tabella."

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/create-table-from-query.php:329
msgid "wpDataTables does not support subqueries or derived tables in FROM. Use a simple table reference, e.g. SELECT * FROM table_name."
msgstr "wpDataTables non supporta subquery o tabelle derivate in FROM. Utilizza un semplice riferimento alla tabella, ad esempio SELECT * FROM nome_tabella."

